{
  "raw": {
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912162643825099~1/edit": {
      "title": "Director, Global Operations",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/11/2026 Department: Global Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV122004#005 Help shape ACU's next phase of international engagement Bring institutional expertise together to deliver on global ambition Full-time, fixed-term (5 year) appointment Based at ACU's North Sydney or Melbourne campus Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a public institution grounded in Catholic tradition, dedicated to academic excellence, human dignity and the common good. With campuses across Australia, a campus in Rome , the Human Flourishing Centre in Indonesia , and an expanding online presence. Guided by Vision 2033 , ACU combines a strong Australian presence with an increasingly connected international footprint. Reporting to the Pro-Vice-Chancellor Global, the Director, Global Operations offers an opportunity to shape how ACU delivers its next phase of international engagement under Vision 2033. Working across faculties and professional portfolios, the Director will turn global strategy into tangible outcomes, from new education partnerships to the development of ACU's offshore activities, while building the models and institutional capability that enable lasting success. A collaborator and integrator, the Director will bring together faculties, professional portfolios and Global teams to deliver shared priorities. The role will connect international initiatives with the University's academic and professional expertise, establish clear responsibilities and strengthen planning, governance, resourcing and performance arrangements across organisational boundaries. Working with academic and professional leaders, the Director will establish and manage the operational arrangements supporting major Global initiatives, including transnational education, international partnerships, the Rome campus, the Human Flourishing Centre and other offshore activities. The role will manage implementation plans and dependencies, resolve barriers to delivery and ensure appropriate oversight of financial, regulatory, operational and reputational risk within its remit. The role may also include responsibility for developing selected international relationships or markets, with scope and priorities agreed with the Pro-Vice-Chancellor Global. Working closely with relevant Global leads, faculties and professional portfolios, the Director will progress opportunities from initial engagement through to implementation. As a key member of the Global leadership team, the Director will provide trusted advice to the Pro-Vice-Chancellor Global and exercise sound judgement about priorities, resources and emerging risks. Success will require the ability to build productive relationships, secure decisions and sustain delivery through competing demands and changing external conditions. ACU is seeking an accomplished leader with a demonstrated record of implementing strategy, shaping operating models and delivering complex initiatives across organisational boundaries. The successful candidate will combine strategic thinking with commercial and financial acumen, strong governance and risk judgement, and a practical approach to building institutional capability. Experience in international education, transnational education or global partnerships will be highly regarded. Candidates may bring relevant experience from higher education or another large, complex organisation with an international remit. A collaborative leadership style, the ability to build shared ownership and a record of leading change will be central to the appointment. ACU has partnered with Kuras Leadership Search for the recruitment of this position. For a confidential discussion or to request a copy of the Candidate Information Pack, please contact Betty Kuras on +61 3 9653 9599 or via email at apply@kurasleadershipsearch.com, quoting job code 2688. Applications close Friday, 6 November 2026. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912143586717499~1/edit": {
      "title": "Team Leader",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Department: PSH Law & Business Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV133865#004 Oversee administrative operations for assigned schools within the FLB Professional Services Hub (PSH). ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Part time, 17.5 hours per week, fixed term role until October 2027 at our North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility. About the role: The Team Leader oversees administrative operations for assigned schools within the Faculty of Law and Business (FLB) Professional Services Hub (PSH), leading the assigned school operation teams in course and student administration, staffing, data analysis & reporting, continuous improvement initiatives, and communication with other PSH Team Leaders and Faculty operational staff. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Wendy Dimond, Director - PSH Law & Business and Theology & Philosophy at: wendy.dimond@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $128,699 - $139,238 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $108,751 - $117,657 (pro rata) pa (HEW 7), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 08-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912143651329199~1/edit": {
      "title": "International Student Advisor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Department: International Student Advisors Location: NSW Campus Location: Blacktown, Australia | North Sydney, Australia | Strathfield, Australia Job No: APTAV105968#001 Support international students throughout their student journey. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, fixed term role until June 2027 at our Blacktown, Strathfield or North Sydney campus. About the role: The International Student Adviser (ISA) supports international students throughout their student journey. The ISA Team works closely with the International Student Transition and Orientation staff in the Education Pathways Directorate to enhance the onboarding experience of international students, maximising acceptance to enrolment conversion and contributing to their retention. The ISA is a key contact point for international students requiring assistance or referral to specialist ACU services such as academic skills, counselling and well-being. The ISA team is responsible for Confirmation of Enrolment (CoE) processing for continuing students. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Candice Ager - International Student Advisors at: candice.ager@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $116,410 - $125,049 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $98,367 - $105,667 (pro rata) pa (HEW 6), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 08-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
