    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912142659346299~1/edit": {
      "title": "Career Educator",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Department: Careers and Employability Location: ACT Campus Location: Canberra, Australia Job No: APTAV116233#009 Deliver personalised student-centred career support and career development initiatives ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Part time, 21 hours per week, (0.6FTE) continuing role, based at our Canberra campus About the role: ACU Career Educators provide high-impact, student-centred career development learning experiences, resources and services that support students to develop the skills, capabilities and confidence to successfully launch and navigate their career journeys. Through direct engagement with students, you'll deliver personalised career support alongside scalable career development initiatives. You will implement ACU's career development learning strategy and, under the direction of the National Manager, deliver career services, co-curricular initiatives, and targeted curriculum-embedded interventions aligned with institutional and faculty priorities. This includes the ongoing development and delivery of career development learning content, learning design projects, academic collaborations and personalised, one-to-one and point-of-need career support services. In undertaking this work, Career Educators apply evidence-based career development theories and best-practice learning design techniques to ensure learning experiences are purposeful, inclusive and responsive to student needs. You will use data and evaluation skills to evidence learning gain, inform continuous improvement and demonstrate impact, while partnering closely with stakeholders to create scalable career development opportunities that enhance graduate employability for all ACU students. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Martin Evans, National Manager, Careers & Employability at: Martin.Evans@acu.edu.au What we offe