      "title": "Administrative Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Department: School of Nursing, Midwifery & Paramed (NSW) Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV106415#023 Exceptional opportunity to provide administrative and coordination services to the National School of Nursing Midwifery & Paramedicine Work collaboratively with a supportive team to deliver ACU's strategic and faculty priorities ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity with some hybrid flexibility working at North Sydney campus About the role: Operating within School of Nursing, Midwifery & Paramedicine (NSW) , the Administrative Officer provides high level administrative and coordination support to all areas of the School of Nursing, Midwifery and Paramedicine. The position is responsible for delivering administrative support to the Heads of School, leadership teams and the wider faculty at the direction of the Team Leader to ensure the efficient operation of the school on a day to day basis. Undertakes reception duties on campus, acts as the first point of contact and resolves enquiries from staff, students, university stakeholders and visitors. Supports faculty academic, administrative and technical staff with key administrative functions and provides timely information and advice. Instructs and coordinates administrative workflows within university requirements and timelines. Develops an understanding of regulations, processes and organisational structures relevant to the functioning of the school. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Hyery Im, Team Leader - School of Nursing, Midwifery & Paramedicine (NSW) at: hyery.im@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $