    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912143588927699~1/edit": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Speech Pathology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Department: Speech Pathology (North Sydney) Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV102103#100 Outstanding Associate Professor opportunity to significantly influence learning and education in the discipline of Speech Pathology Join a highly recognised national school and work closely with colleagues to enhance the student experience ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, continuing opportunity working at North Sydney campus About the role: Operating within Speech Pathology (North Sydney) , the Associate Professor, Speech Pathology, a teaching and research focused role, will provide leadership, make outstanding and original contributions to learning, education, scholarship and research, and drive enhancement of the student experience at ACU in the discipline of Speech Pathology. The position will be responsible for course coordination and impact the development and implementation of the Bachelor of Speech Pathology course by providing theoretical and clinical teaching and research. Working collaboratively with the Head of School, Deputy Head of School, National Head of Discipline, Course Coordinators and other staff as required the Associate Professor will ensure that the delivery of the curriculum is comprehensively managed. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Erin Conway, Professor, Speech Pathology - School of Allied Health at: Erin.Conway@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $202,272 - $222,654 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $171,352 - $188,772 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level D), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 11-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equi