    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912156712082999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Assurance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Department: Assurance Unit Location: NSW,QLD,VIC Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a young and dynamic institution making a significant impact. Founded on the principles of Catholic social teaching, it aims to promote academic excellence, serve communities, and act as a catalyst for positive change. Ranked in the top two per cent of universities worldwide and in the top 10 Catholic universities, the university has seven campuses around Australia, a campus in Rome, Italy, and an online campus - ACU Online. ACU's Vision 2033 presents a strategy which allows students and staff to respond to the needs of a changing world while working to enable flourishing lives, foster thriving communities and forge an ethical future. Based in either Sydney, Melbourne, or Brisbane and reporting directly to the General Counsel and Chief Legal, Assurance and Governance Officer, the Associate Director, Assurance is responsible for strengthening ACU's assurance capability by leading a coordinated, risk-based program of assurance activities across enterprise risk management, compliance monitoring, internal audit and internal review; with oversight of institutional quality and regulatory readiness (including TEQSA). The role provides strategic advice, timely reporting and independent insight to support transparency, accountability and informed decision-making, including through reporting to the Vice-Chancellor's Management Committee (VCMC), the Audit & Risk Committee (and other governance committees as required) and the monitoring and validation of remediation actions. The Associate Director builds organisational capability and maturity in self-assurance practices, supports consistent evidence and documentation standards, and promotes continuous improvement across the university. We are seeking candidates with inclusive leadership skills and experience in a large, complex, and preferably regulated organisation. The successful candidate will be a highly collaborative and mission-led professional who will work with colleagues across other central service functions and the academic community to drive enterprise-wide transformation in Assurance and Risk. For a confidential discussion or to request the candidate information booklet, please contact Kate Robinson on +61 409 769 560 or at krobinson@robinsonfitzgerald.com.au or Janine Fitzgerald on +61 424 164 765 or at jfitzgerald@robinsonfitzgerald.com.au quoting reference RF0274. Applications can be sent to either or both of the above email addresses and will close on 11 November 2026. ACU is not accepting applications submitted through this recruitment portal. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912141481584799~1/edit": {
      "title": "Student Life Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Department: Student Life Location: NSW Campus Location: Blacktown | NSW Job No: APTAV102864#012 Enhance the student experience through the delivery of student engagement programs and events ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Part time (3 days per week), continuing role based on our Blacktown campus About the role: As a Student Life Officer, you'll be the first point of contact for students seeking information about the range of Student Experience services and act as the Blacktown campus representative of the Student Life Unit. You'll work closely with students and other key stakeholders to organise, promote and deliver student engagement programs, events and activities that enhance the student experience. You'll deliver a range of extracurricular, social and sport programs, events and activities that create vibrancy and encourage a sense of belonging to an inclusive and diverse community that is committed to justice, equity and the common good. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Jodie Beckmann, National Manager, Student Life at: jodie.beckmann@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $112,625 - $120,977 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $95,170 - $102,227 (pro rata) pa (HEW 6), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 12-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912142531230399~1/edit": {
      "title": "Executive Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Department: Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Catholic Mission) Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney Job No: APTAV118410#011 Provide high-level administrative, digital and project support across the Office of the Deputy Vice Chancellor (Catholic Mission). ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Full time, fixed term role until September 2027 at our North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility. About the role: Operating within the Portfolio of Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Catholic Mission) , the Executive Officer provides high-level administrative, digital and project support across the Office of the Deputy Vice Chancellor (Catholic Mission), including support to the Identity and Mission Directorate and Associate Director, Mission and Ministry. The role is directly responsible for the effective coordination of the Deputy Vice Chancellor's diary, travel and meeting coordination. The incumbent also undertakes event coordination support, finance and procurement processes, stakeholder communications, and the development of digital and print resources that support faith formation, spirituality, engagement in the Catholic intellectual tradition, and the broader mission and identity of the University. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Catherine Le Mottee, Senior Advisor, Policy & Projects - Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Catholic Mission) at: catherine.lemottee@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $116,410 - $125,049 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $98,367 - $105,667 (pro rata) pa (HEW 6), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 12-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912148624881599~1/edit": {
      "title": "AskACU Centre Service Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Department: AskACU Centre - QLD/ACT Location: QLD Campus Location: Brisbane, Australia Job No: APTAV129152#003 Provide quality customer service support to current and prospective students. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. If you're passionate about helping others, thrive in a fast-paced environment, and want to make a real difference in a student's journey, then this is the role for you! Full time, continuing role at our Brisbane campus. About the role: Working as part of a national team, the AskACU Service Officer provides quality customer service support to current and prospective students and staff on a range of topics. Working in the AskACU Centre, the AskACU Service Officer (AskACU Centre) responds to enquiries by face-to-face, email, phone, live chat, and other enquiry-types as appropriate. The position-holder is responsible for case-management of enquiries and being the first point of call for the ACU Community. This position ensures students and staff receive a positive customer service experience on campus by resolving issues, providing relevant services and supporting high level enquiry management. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Kirsty Krishna, Coordinator - AskACU Centres at: Kirsty.Krishna@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $104,877 - $113,049 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $88,621 - $95,940 (pro rata) pa (HEW 5), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 12-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply