    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912140585796599~1/edit": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Department: Thomas More Law School Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV135499#003 Make outstanding and original contributions to learning and teaching, scholarship and research within the Thomas More Law School. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, continuing role at our North Sydney campus. About the role: Operating within Thomas More Law School the Associate Professor will make outstanding and original contributions to learning and teaching, scholarship and research within the school. The role will contribute to the strategic direction of the school, lead new curriculum and pedagogical developments including online teaching as well as higher degree student supervision. The incumbent will have the opportunity to undertake significant leadership roles in the school and contribute to the wider university. The incumbent will also make an outstanding contribution to the governance of academic programs in law. They will also build relationships with external organisations and communities. As well as providing disciplinary leadership, the Associate Professor will make significant contributions to quality improvement of programs including ensuring the implementation of assurance of learning activities, mentorship of staff in the learning, teaching and research activity of the school and in the development, implementation and accreditation of the curricula. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Lidia Xynas, Dean, Thomas More Law School at: lidia.xynas@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $209,060 - $230,113 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $177,116 - $195,110 (pro rata)