    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912140586963699~1/edit": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Migration Law)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Department: Thomas More Law School Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV135499#002 Develop and deliver high quality, innovative teaching in Migration Law and related Public Law subjects. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Full time, continuing role at our North Sydney or Melbourne campus. About the role: Operating within Thomas More Law School , the Lecturer Law will be accountable for high-quality teaching and learning outcomes through the development, delivery and continuous improvement of lectures, tutorials and workshops in a number of subjects in Migration Law and related Public Law subjects. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Lidia Xynas, Dean, Thomas More Law School at: lidia.xynas@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $147,424 - $173,913 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $124, - $147,076 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level B), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your c