    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912140588540599~1/edit": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Law)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Department: Thomas More Law School Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV135499#001 Provide high quality teaching and learning outcomes through the development, delivery and continuous improvement of lectures, tutorials and workshops in the Law discipline. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Full time, continuing role at our North Sydney or Melbourne campus. About the role: Operating within Thomas More Law School , the incumbent will be accountable for high quality teaching and learning outcomes through the development, delivery and continuous improvement of lectures, tutorials and workshops in a number of the following core subjects in Law: Foundations of Law and Legal Research, Contracts, Torts, Property, Statutory Interpretation, Evidence, Legal Ethics and Professional Responsibility, International Law, Administrative Law, Public Law, Land Law, Civil Procedure and Alternative Dispute Resolution, Constitutional Law, Equity and Trusts and Legal Theory. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Lidia Xynas, Dean, Thomas More Law School at: lidia.xynas@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $147,424 - $173,913 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $124,574 - $147,076 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level B), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not 