    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912150469327199~1/edit": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Biblical Studies and Classical Hebrew)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/11/2026 Department: National School of Theology Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV129377#022 Provide academic expertise to ensure excellence in teaching and learning and research ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, continuing role based at our North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility About the role: The appointment of a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in the area of biblical studies and classical Hebrew, arises from a generous philanthropic donation for the purposes of advancing common objectives with the university for growth in the named discipline areas. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Biblical Studies and Classical Hebrew will provide academic expertise in the School of Theology, Faculty of Theology and Philosophy, to ensure excellence in teaching and learning within biblical studies and classical Hebrew and undertake and lead research in this field. It is expected that the appointee to this position will contribute to the mission of the school, faculty and university through teaching, research, academic administration, curriculum development, program coordination, and working collaboratively across the faculty and the university and with external partners. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Belinda Malone, Executive Officer, Faculty of Theology & Philosophy at: Belinda.Malone@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $142,635 - $168,287 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $120,529 - $142,305 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level B), OR $178,482 - $193,772 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $151,018 - $164,087 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level C), employer contri