    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912135456138799~1/edit": {
      "title": "Functional & Business Analyst",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/11/2026 Department: Workforce Systems Administration Location: QLD Campus Location: Brisbane, Australia Job No: APTAV115261#005 Provide functional leadership and strategic advice across ACU's workforce systems environment Join high performing team delivering system administration and operational support to people management functions ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity with some hybrid flexibility working at Brisbane campus About the role: Operating within Workforce Systems Administration , the Functional & Business Analyst will provide functional leadership, consultation and strategic advice across ACU's workforce systems environment. The position will understand and be informed by business needs, lead business analysis, facilitate stakeholder engagement and influence the design of innovative, sustainable workforce solutions that support the university's strategic priorities. Acting as the primary functional interface between People & Capability, new Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) Program and external vendors the Business Analyst will apply deep knowledge and expertise in HRIS, payroll and workforce business processes, systems and training, and change management to improve service delivery, support the ERP transformation and ensure workforce systems continue to meet the university's operational, legislative and future business needs. Previous experience and knowledge of managing workforce/people or HRIS platforms, systems integration and ERP programs using Workday, Aurion, SAP, Oracle or similar large-scale systems is highly desirable. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Sam Silva, Manager, Workforce Systems at: sam.silva@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $138,111 - $154,409 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $116,706 - $130,478 (pro rata) pa (HEW 8), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 18-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underp