    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912134586265399~1/edit": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/11/2026 Department: Graduate Research School Location: VIC Campus Location: Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV113103#029 Provide high-level administrative support services to support graduate research students, staff and external stakeholders within the Graduate Research School. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Full time, continuing role at our Melbourne campus with some hybrid flexibility. About the role: Operating within Graduate Research School , reporting to the Graduate Research Coordinator, the Graduate Research Officer provides high-level administrative support services to support graduate research students, staff and external stakeholders within the Graduate Research School. The position has primary responsibility of administrative activities across the student life cycle from initial enquiry through to course completion, including the provision of expert advice and exceptional customer service. The position actively engages in a case management approach to solve complex issues, undertake high level administrative tasks, communicate with a range of internal and external stakeholders, help identify areas for improvements and support the implementation of new systems and processes. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Lisa Lavey, Manager, Research Operations - Research Office at: lisa.lavey@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $116,410 - $125,049 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $98,367 - $105,667 (pro rata) pa (HEW 6), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equi