    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912135626164999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator - CTC Partners",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/11/2026 Department: Faculty of Theology & Philosophy Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV129377#024 Provide project oversight of the ACU-Catholic Theological College (CTC) Steering Committee ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, fixed term (12 months) role based at our Melbourne or North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility About the role: As the Project Coordinator - CTC Partnerships, you'll provide executive support to, and project oversight of, the ACU-Catholic Theological College (CTC) Steering Committee in its strategic leadership and decision-making related to Project Unitas. The Project Manager operates across and contributes to all six workstreams (governance and legal; academic assurance; space and facilities; finance; people; and communications and stakeholders), ensuring timely progress of discussions, following up on action points for each, keeping the Steering Committee well informed at all stages, facilitating consultation with internal and external stakeholders and timely decision making, and helping the committee manage strategic risks and dependencies. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Belinda Malone, Executive Officer, Faculty of Theology & Philosophy at: Belinda.Malone@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $124,509 - $134,699 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $105,212 - $113,823 (pro rata) pa (HEW 7), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 22-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912135575029599~1/edit": {
      "title": "Faculty Governance Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/11/2026 Department: Faculty of Theology & Philosophy Location: NSW,QLD,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Strathfield, Australia | Brisbane, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV137700#002 Provide professional governance and administrative support to the Faculty of Theology and Philosophy ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Part time (0.5FTE), continuing role based at our North Sydney, Strathfield, Melbourne or Brisbane campus with some hybrid flexibility About the role: As the Faculty Governance Officer, you'll provide professional governance and administrative support to the Faculty of Theology and Philosophy to ensure the effective operation of the faculty's governance framework, committees and decision-making processes. You will coordinate governance activities, ensure compliance with university policies and procedures, maintain governance records and facilitate the timely preparation and distribution of committee documentation and reports. Working closely with the Executive Dean, Director, Strategy and Operations, academic leaders and professional staff, you'll support the faculty's academic governance, strategic planning and operational objectives through the provision of high-quality governance advice, secretariat services and administrative coordination. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Michael Robertson, Director, Strategy and Operations, PSH Law & Business and Theology & Philosophy at: michael.robertson@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $124,509 - $134,699 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $105,212 - $113,823 (pro rata) pa (HEW 7), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 25-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912140659661499~1/edit": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Professor (Nursing)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/11/2026 Department: National School of Nursing, Midwifery & Paramed Location: VIC Campus Location: Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV104349#029 Lead nursing research that transforms clinical care and patient outcomes Unite academic and clinical expertise through a powerful joint appointment Shape a research program and inspire the next generation of nurse researcher Australian Catholic University (ACU) and St Vincent’s Hospital Melbourne share a commitment to improving lives through excellence in education, research and compassionate care. Their partnership connects academic expertise with clinical practice to advance nursing research and deliver better outcomes for patients and communities. ACU’s National School of Nursing, Midwifery and Paramedicine brings together a substantial national network of educators and researchers. St Vincent’s Hospital Melbourne is a leading teaching, research and tertiary health service. Together with the Nursing Research Institute, they provide a collaborative environment for nurse-led, multidisciplinary research with practical impact. About the opportunity: This joint appointment offers an exceptional opportunity to shape a clinically relevant nursing research program at the intersection of academia and healthcare. Working across ACU and St Vincent’s Hospital Melbourne, you will lead health services research focused on translating evidence into clinical practice to improve patient outcomes and health systems. You will strengthen connections between clinicians and academics, develop collaborative research partnerships and attract competitive funding to support significant new projects. A central focus will be building research capability through mentoring clinicians and emerging researchers, supervising higher degree research students and supporting a collegiate, high-performing research culture. You will also contribute to scholarship, teaching and the broader academic and professional life of both organisations. Based at ACU’s St Patrick’s campus and St Vincent’s Hospital Melbourne, this full-time appointment is offered on a fixed-term basis to April 2028, with the opportunity for extension subject to funding and performance. About you: You are a collaborative nursing academic who combines research credibility with a clear commitment to improving clinical care. You bring: A doctoral qualification in nursing or an equivalent discipline, and current unrestricted AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse. A strong research profile, demonstrated through high-quality publications and success in securing and leading competitive research grants. Expertise relevant to health services research, evidence-based nursing practice and translating research into improved care. Experience leading multidisciplinary research and building productive partnerships across academic and clinical settings. A commitment to developing others through research training, mentoring and supervision of higher degree research students. Strategic judgement, strong communication skills and the ability to influence stakeholders and lead change. Alignment with the mission and values of ACU and St Vincent’s, including a commitment to human dignity, compassion and the common good. For a confidential discussion, please contact Marcus Engeman at Hoffmann Reed on 0431 804 418 or marcus@hoffmannreed.com.au To apply, email your cover letter, comprehensive CV and a response addressing the selection criteria (maximum two pages) to confidential@hoffmannreed.com.au. Applications close: Monday 30 November 2026. ACU is not accepting applications via this recruitment portal. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    }
  },
